  "raw": {
    "https://www.monmouthcollege.edu/offices/hr/employment-opportunities/#tenure-track-political-science-professor": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Political Science Professor",
      "description": "Monmouth College Monmouth, Illinois July 1, 2026 The political science program at Monmouth College invites applications for an Assistant Professor in American Politics, beginning Fall 2027. We seek candidates with broad expertise in political science; specialization in American Politics and interest in supporting our pre-Law program are preferred. The successful candidate will teach courses, advise and mentor undergraduates, help build the program, and participate in shared governance. A completed PhD is required prior to the start of the appointment. The political science program is housed in the School of Humanities and Civic Engagement, which pairs the depths of the humanities and social sciences. The school’s animating commitments are critical thinking, the broad perspectives of the liberal arts, and real-world societal impact. Faculty have opportunities to participate in interdisciplinary programs, such as women’s studies. Though small, our program sends graduates regularly into strong law and graduate programs and into careers in Illinois politics. Located in west central Illinois about 200 miles from Chicago, Monmouth College is a vibrant residential college dedicated to empowering students to lead meaningful lives and successful careers. We foster a supportive, collaborative, mission-driven workplace where faculty and staff are valued partners in student success. Average class size is 14, with a 12:1 student-to-faculty ratio. More information about the College, its mission, and its curricula is available on the College’s website. Review of applications begins September 15, 2026; the search remains open until the position is filled. Applicants should submit a cover letter addressing courses they are prepared to teach and their scholarly interests, a curriculum vitae, and a list of three references to Deena.McLaughlin , Assistant Director of Human Resources. Monmouth College EOE/Nondiscrimination Statement"
    },
    "https://www.monmouthcollege.edu/offices/hr/employment-opportunities/#part-time-adjunct-religious-studies": {
      "title": "Part-Time Adjunct - Religious Studies",
      "description": "Monmouth College Monmouth, Illinois March 25, 2026 School of Humanities and Civic Engagement - Religious Studies – Part-Time Adjunct Monmouth College, an independent residential liberal arts institution in Illinois, seeks applications for adjuncts in the area of Religious Studies. The position reports to the chair of the School of Humanities and Civic Engagement, and the Vice President for Academic Affairs and Dean of the Faculty. The position has daily contact with students, staff, faculty, and persons outside the campus community. The successful candidate will be a dynamic colleague willing to work closely with undergraduate students and members of the School of Humanities and Civic Engagement. The candidate will teach one or two religious studies class as part of Monmouth elective offerings. Preference is for on-campus in-person teaching, but hybrid or online teaching considered. Required: An M.A. in Religious Studies or related Field is required for appointment as an adjunct instructor. A commitment to the liberal arts and an appreciation for the small college learning environment is essential. Salary Range: $4000-$5000 per credit course dependent upon qualifications To apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy and names and contact information of three references who can speak to your qualifications. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Please send all materials electronically to Deena McLaughlin . Located in west central Illinois about 200 miles from Chicago, Monmouth College is a vibrant residential liberal arts college dedicated to empowering students to lead meaningful lives and successful careers. As an employer, we foster a supportive, collaborative, and mission-driven workplace where faculty and staff are valued partners in shaping student success. The average class size at Monmouth College is 14 students, with a 12:1 student to faculty ratio. For more information about the College, please see our mission statement . More information about our core and departmental curricula and the College may be found on the College’s website . Monmouth College EOE/Nondiscrimination Statement"
    },
    "https://www.monmouthcollege.edu/offices/hr/employment-opportunities/#part-time-adjunct-biology": {
      "title": "Part-Time Adjunct -  Biology",
      "description": "Monmouth College Monmouth, Illinois March 25, 2026 School of Health and Natural Sciences- Biology – Part-Time Adjunct Monmouth College, an independent residential liberal arts institution in Illinois, seeks applications for adjuncts in Biology, particularly Botany, and Environmental Studies. The position reports to the Chair of the School of Health and Natural Sciences, and the Vice President for Academic Affairs and Dean of the Faculty. The position has daily contact with students, staff, faculty, and persons outside the campus community. The successful candidate will be a dynamic colleague willing to work closely with undergraduate students and members of the School of Health and Natural Sciences. The candidate will teach one to two biology classes as part of Monmouth elective offerings. Preference is for on-campus in-person teaching, but hybrid or online teaching considered. Required: An M.A. in Biology or related field is required for appointment as an adjunct instructor. A commitment to the liberal arts and an appreciation for the small college learning environment is essential. Salary Range: $4000-$5000 per credit course dependent upon qualifications To apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy and names and contact information of three references who can speak to your qualifications. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Please send all materials electronically to Deena McLaughlin . Located in west central Illinois about 200 miles from Chicago, Monmouth College is a vibrant residential liberal arts college dedicated to empowering students to lead meaningful lives and successful careers. As an employer, we foster a supportive, collaborative, and mission-driven workplace where faculty and staff are valued partners in shaping student success. The average class size at Monmouth College is 14 students, with a 12:1 student to faculty ratio. For more information about the College, please see our mission statement . More information about our core and departmental curricula and the College may be found on the College’s website . Monmouth College EOE/Nondiscrimination Statement"
    },
