      "description": "Monmouth College Monmouth, Illinois March 25, 2026 School of Humanities and Civic Engagement- History – Part-Time Adjunct Monmouth College, an independent residential liberal arts institution in Illinois, seeks applications for adjuncts in the area of History. The position reports to the Chair of the School of Humanities and Civic Engagement, and the Vice President for Academic Affairs and Dean of the Faculty. The position has daily contact with students, staff, faculty, and persons outside the campus community. The successful candidate will be a dynamic colleague willing to work closely with undergraduate students and members of the School of Humanities and Civic Engagement. The candidate will teach one or two history classes as part of Monmouth elective offerings. Preference is for on-campus in-person teaching, but hybrid or online teaching considered. Required: An M.A. in History or related Field is required for appointment as an adjunct instructor. A commitment to the liberal arts and an appreciation for the small college learning environment is essential. Salary Range: $4000-$5000 per credit course dependent upon qualifications To apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy and names and contact information of three references who can speak to your qualifications. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Please send all materials electronically to Deena McLaughlin . Located in west central Illinois about 200 miles from Chicago, Monmouth College is a vibrant residential liberal arts college dedicated to empowering students to lead meaningful lives and successful careers. As an employer, we foster a supportive, collaborative, and mission-driven workplace where faculty and staff are valued partners in shaping student success. The average class size at Monmouth College is 14 students, with a 12:1 student to faculty ratio. For more information about the