    "https://www.monmouthcollege.edu/offices/hr/employment-opportunities/#preservice-teacher-education-generalist-position": {
      "title": "Preservice Teacher Education Generalist Position",
      "description": "Monmouth College Monmouth, Illinois March 2026 Monmouth College’s School of Education and Human Development seeks applications for a tenure track, assistant level generalist position in Preservice Teacher Education within the School of Education and Human Development beginning August 2026. Preservice Teacher Education currently encompasses approximately a quarter of the Monmouth College students within its elementary, secondary, and PK-12 licensure programs. Successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate candidate courses within the preservice teacher education program. Applicants must possess comprehensive knowledge of elementary &/or secondary level pedagogy. Successful applicants must be committed to excellence in teaching, be adept at using contemporary instructional technology, and be willing to collaborate with the community and area schools to form productive relationships. Preference will be given to candidates with backgrounds in Educational Foundations; Content-Area Literacy; Clinical Supervision; and/or Instructional Technology. Faculty teach six to eight courses annually, advise undergraduate students, and supervise candidates in field experiences. The successful applicant must demonstrate strong potential for excellent teaching, service in a liberal arts college setting, and academic scholarship. Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D./Ed.D. in Teacher Education, or other closely related field. Preference will be given to applicants who are qualified to teach in additional content areas, have prior experience in institutions of higher education, and have at least five years of full-time teaching experience in PK-12 or equivalent classroom settings. The successful candidate must be committed to undergraduate teaching excellence, scholarship, academic advising, and the College’s liberal arts mission. Monmouth College aspires to be the home of an inclusive community of students, teacher/scholars and staff working as a team for the benefit of the students. Salary range for this position is $55,000 - $57,000 with attractive benefits package including health plan with dental and vision, retirement plan, and tuition benefits for eligible dependents. To apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy and names and contact information of three references who can speak to your qualifications. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Please send all materials electronically to the Search Committee Chair: Dr. Tiffany Springer at dmclaughlin@monmouthcollege.edu . Please use “Education and Human Development search” as the subject line. Located in west central Illinois about 200 miles from Chicago, Monmouth College is a vibrant residential liberal arts college dedicated to empowering students to lead meaningful lives and successful careers. As an employer, we foster a supportive, collaborative, and mission-driven workplace where faculty and staff are valued partners in shaping student success. The average class size at Monmouth College is 14 students, with a 12:1 student to faculty ratio. For more information about the College, please see our mission statement . More information about our core and departmental curricula and the College may be found on the College’s website . Monmouth College EOE/Nondiscrimination Statement"
    },
    "https://www.monmouthcollege.edu/offices/hr/employment-opportunities/#tenure-track-marketing-professor": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Marketing Professor",
      "description": "Monmouth College Monmouth, Illinois Nov. 20, 2025 High-impact and industry-connected, with a long legacy of successful students, the Monmouth College School of Business continues its search for a Marketing specialist to help lead a new and rapidly growing program. The successful candidate will teach core marketing courses and help us build in areas including digital marketing, marketing research, and marketing analytics. At a minimum, candidates will possess: · a master’s degree in marketing or a closely related field · practical knowledge of marketing · the strong potential for teaching excellence, and · the desire to shape, deliver, and lead a relevant, engaging curriculum to undergraduate students The successful candidate will be motivated to direct this popular new venture toward what the next generation of students will need to thrive in their careers, including use of disruptive technology and AI integration. About the School of Business As Monmouth’s largest program for nearly twenty years, offering majors in accounting, business administration, economics, and now marketing, the School of Business has taught generations of talented students, turning them into successful industry leaders. Located in the welcoming community of Monmouth, Illinois, the college is a member of the prestigious Associated Colleges of the Midwest. Monmouth is in the top tier of U.S. News & World Report’s Best Colleges for National Liberal Arts Colleges, is ranked 70 th out of 240 schools in the “National Universities – Liberal Arts” category by Washington Monthly and was recognized in the top 5% of U.S. Colleges by College Factual for colleges that provide value for students. Expected salary range: $80,000 - $100,000. Review of applications will begin immediately and proceed until the position is filled. To apply, please send by email a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, a statement of research/professional development interests, and a list of three references to: Deena McLaughlin. . Monmouth College EOE/Nondiscrimination Statement Staff positions"
    },
    "https://www.monmouthcollege.edu/offices/hr/employment-opportunities/#associate-director-of-prospect-development-and-donor-relatio": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Prospect Development and Donor Relations",
      "description": "MONMOUTH COLLEGE MONMOUTH, ILLINOIS September 4, 2026 Monmouth College seeks applications for the position of Associate Director of Prospect Development and Donor Relations. This position supports Monmouth College’s fundraising efforts by providing strategic prospect research, portfolio and pipeline management, donor relations, and direct donor engagement for the Office of Development and College Relations. The position plays an important role in strengthening relationships with donors through personalized stewardship, endowed fund reporting, donor communications, events, and other engagement activities that demonstrate the impact of philanthropy at Monmouth College. View full position description here . Competitive salary and attractive benefit package, including retirement plan, health and dental insurance plan, and certain tuition benefits for eligible dependents. Applications will be accepted until position filled or search closed. Send letter of application, resume and the names and telephone numbers of three references to Deena McLaughlin . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Monmouth College EOE/Nondiscrimination Statement"
    },
    "https://www.monmouthcollege.edu/offices/hr/employment-opportunities/#assistant-softball-coach": {
      "title": "Assistant Softball Coach",
      "description": "MONMOUTH COLLEGE MONMOUTH, ILLINOIS JULY 2026 Monmouth College seeks applications for the position of Assistant Softball Coach (Positional Experience). Reporting to the Head Softball Coach, then to the Director of Athletics, the Assistant Softball Coach is responsible for assisting the softball program, as well as being committed to the academic mission of the College. The Assistant Softball Coach teaches the sport of softball to student athletes, and provides for the coaching, recruitment and retention of softball players to the college. Specific emphasis on pitching, fielding, hitting and strength and conditioning. This position will also provide administrative support to the Athletics Department of up to 10 hours per week on average. Review full position description here . Monmouth College is a vibrant residential liberal arts college dedicated to empowering students to lead meaningful lives and successful careers. As an employer, we foster a supportive, collaborative, and mission-driven workplace where faculty and staff are valued partners in shaping student success. Applications will be accepted until position filled or search closed. Send letter of application, resume, and three references to: Deena McLaughlin . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Monmouth College EOE/Nondiscrimination Statement"
    },
    "https://www.monmouthcollege.edu/offices/hr/employment-opportunities/#assistant-soccer-coach-men-and-women": {
      "title": "Assistant Soccer Coach- Men and Women",
      "description": "MONMOUTH COLLEGE MONMOUTH, ILLINOIS JUNE 2026 Monmouth College seeks applications for the position of Assistant Soccer Coach. Reporting to the Head Soccer Coaches, then to the Director of Athletics, the Assistant Soccer Coach is responsible for assisting both the men’s and women’s soccer programs, as well as being committed to the academic mission of the College. The Assistant Soccer Coach teaches the sport of soccer to student athletes, and provides for the coaching, recruitment and retention of soccer players to the college. Specific emphasis on strength and conditioning. Review full position description here Monmouth College is a vibrant residential liberal arts college dedicated to empowering students to lead meaningful lives and successful careers. As an employer, we foster a supportive, collaborative, and mission-driven workplace where faculty and staff are valued partners in shaping student success. Applications will be accepted until position filled or search closed. Send letter of application, resume and the names and telephone numbers of three references to: Deena McLaughlin . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Monmouth College EOE/Nondiscrimination Statement"
    },
    "https://www.monmouthcollege.edu/offices/hr/employment-opportunities/#part-time-campus-safety-officer": {
      "title": "Part-time Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "MONMOUTH COLLEGE MONMOUTH, ILLINOIS January 28, 2026 Monmouth College, an independent residential liberal arts institution in Illinois, seeks applications for the position of Part-time Campus Safety Officer. The Campus Safety Officer reports to the Senior Campus Safety Officer who reports to the Assistant Vice President for Student Affairs. The position is responsible for a variety of safety and security procedures on campus. Campus Safety Officers have daily contact with students, staff, faculty, and people outside the campus community. Review the full position description here . Monmouth College is a vibrant residential liberal arts college dedicated to empowering students to lead meaningful lives and successful careers. As an employer, we foster a supportive, collaborative, and mission-driven workplace where faculty and staff are valued partners in shaping student success. Send letter of application, resume and the names and contact information of three references to: Deena McLaughlin . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Monmouth College EOE/Nondiscrimination Statement"
    },
    "https://www.monmouthcollege.edu/offices/hr/employment-opportunities/#men-s-and-women-s-swimming-assistant-coach": {
      "title": "Men’s and Women’s Swimming- Assistant Coach",
      "description": "MONMOUTH COLLEGE MONMOUTH, ILLINOIS AUGUST 12, 2025 Monmouth College seeks applications for the part-time, temporary position of Assistant Men’s and Women’s Swimming Coach. This position reports to the Head Swimming Coach to the Director of Athletics, then to the President. Candidate is responsible for assisting in all aspects of the swimming program, as well as being committed to the academic mission of the College. The Assistant Swimming Coach assists in planning, supervision and administration of all aspects of the Men’s and Women’s Swimming Program. Experience as a swimmer or swimming coach is desired. Complete job description can be found here . Applications will be accepted until position filled or search closed. Send letter of application, resume, and three references to Deena McLaughlin . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Monmouth College admits students of any race, religion, color, sex, national or ethnic origin to all rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to Monmouth students. Monmouth College EOE/Nondiscrimination Statement Monmouth College EOE/Nondiscrimination Statement For Student Employment Opportunities click here Related Links Human Resources Employment Opportunities Employee Resources & Forms UMR Transparency Transparency in Coverage Contact Us Offices & Services Employment Opportunities Maps & Directions Library Contact Us Legal Consumer Information Editor Login <li><span href=\"#copyright\" aria-label=\"Copyright 2026 Monmouth College\" title=\"Copyright 2026 Monmouth College\"><i class=\"far fa-copyright\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></li> Copyright 2026 Monmouth College Monmouth College 700 E Broadway Monmouth, IL 61462 (309) 457-2345 Back to top START FOOTER SCRIPTS END FOOTER SCRIPTS"
    }
  },
